#!/usr/bin/env python3
#
# wsdata: data source and renderer for the wallstreet widgets
#
# The pages wallstreet used to scrape (Yahoo Finance, WSJ, Reuters feeds)
# are gone or refuse non-browser clients.  This helper fetches market
# movers from the Nasdaq API and headlines and pictures from the RSS feeds
# listed in newsboat.urls, caches them for a short while so that several
# panes share one request, and renders them for the widgets.
#
#   wsdata table                     coloured quote table
#   wsdata movers up|down            one line of gainers / losers
#   wsdata headlines                 one headline per line
#   wsdata image                     path of a random downloaded picture
#   wsdata browse                    the quote table, interactive: click a row or
#                                    move with the arrow keys to select a stock,
#                                    "/" searches a stock and adds it to the watchlist
#   wsdata chart                     price chart of the selected stock, follows
#                                    the selection; 1-4 or a click change the span
#   wsdata logo                      logo of the selected stock, follows the selection
#   wsdata cachedir                  path of the private cache directory
#   wsdata demofeed                  write the demo feed, print its urls file
#
# With WALLSTREET_DEMO=1 nothing is fetched: quotes, headlines and the picture
# are invented (companies that do not exist), for screenshots, tests and
# machines without a network.
#   wsdata marquee COLOR DELAY TEXT  scroll TEXT once across the terminal
